Z||000014||Raydar||12-29-1999||10:35 AM||||Cooter... (Slightly off-topic) The Monte Carlo SS wheels and 81 Z-28 wheels are not the same, although they look identical. The offset differs by 1/2". Found out the hard way, when my upper control arms cleaned all the weights off the back of the Z-28 wheels.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR>BTW... The 14" Fiero wheels -the ones that look like the original Grand-Am wheels, also differ by 1/2" in offset. <P><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 12-29-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||TOM||12-29-1999||12:28 PM||||I have a mustang with Z rims and it did the same thing. Wiped all the weight off the back side. I just ground a little of the control arm off. But you could just put the weights on the front or use stick ons||||reg||1
