Z||000024||V6pack||12-30-1999||06:27 PM||||Well, now it is my turn. I'm the poor unfortunate that listed these wheels. I picked them up in a eBay auction in Sept. from a description similar to the one I used last week. Shortly after my listing I got one query about the origin of the wheels.  I sent that party and any subsequent other inquiring e-mailer everything I had on them. The 1st person wrote back that he found no reason to doubt they were prototypes, and he also 'copied' a legendary Fiero Guru with his appraisal.  <P>Thus fortified, I also started sending his attachment along to interested persons and doubters.  When I got the fourth doubting query (via the high Bidder) after his 'sneak attack' bid retraction....I ended the auction.  <P>As it turns out, it appears that Scott2m4 has put up a 16" wheel here that solves the mystery and I thank him for that. I don't doubt his picture anymore than  I doubted the guy I got them from.<P>I have taken some %^*# about false advertisement and 'wool' over the eyes. If anything, I may be a little gullable to have beleived the guy I got them from. There certainly was no intent to decieve on my part.  Sorry for the really long post and my public apologies to FD, and others who went out on a limb. to defend my 'doorstops'.  Case closed. <BR>Dave ||||reg||12
